# Data comparison within one unit

Verifies equality and ordering between two byte measures without any unit scaling. Comparing 512B against 1024B exercises `==`, `!=`, `<`, and `>`, while the reflexive `<=` and `>=` cases pin the boundary where both operands are equal.

>>> source
small: int = 512B
large: int = 1024B
print(small == large)
print(small != large)
print(small < large)
print(large > small)
print(small <= small)
print(large >= large)

<<< stdout
false
true
true
true
true
true

<<< stderr
